$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of rutin derivative (quercetin-CF3) A solution of 50 mg (0.08
mmol) of rutin and 11 mg (0.04 mmol) of
2-chloro-5-(trifluoromethyl)-1,3-dinitrobenzene in 5 ml the
N,N-dimethylformamide (DMF) was stirred with K2CO3 (100 mg) for 15 h at
80-90°C. Then, the solution was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 15 ml)
and water (20 ml). The organic phase was separated, and the water phase
was washed three times with ethyl acetate. Combined organic phase was
evaporated in a rotary evaporator, and the solid was dried under reduced
pressure. The product (quercetin-CF3) was obtained. Yield 90%. M.p.
143-145°C. 1H-NMR (DMSO-d6, TMS) δ [ppm] 6.17 (d, 1H, J= 2.0 Hz, C-6),
6.39 (d, 1H, J= 2.0 Hz, C-8), 6.87 (d, 1H, J= 8.3 Hz, C-5'), 7.53 (dd,
1H, J= 2.0, 8.3 Hz, C-6'), 7.66 (d, 1H, J= 2.0 Hz, C-2'), 8.1 (s, 2H,
C-3'' and C-5''). 13C-NMR (DMSO-d6, TMS) 93.8 (C-8), 98.6 (C-6), 103.5
(C-10), 115.5 (C-2'), 116.1 (C-5'), 120.4 (C-6'), 122.1 (CF3), 122.4
(C-1'), 126.8 (C-4''), 126.9 (C-3'' and C-5''), 136.2 (C-3), 143.1
(C-1''), 145.5 (C-3'), 147.3 (C-4'), 148.2 (C-2'' and C-6''), 156.6
(C-9), 157.1 (C-2), 161.2 (C-5), 164.3 (C-7), 176.3 (C-4). APSI-MS [m/z]
575 (M + K)+ (575.00 calculated for C22H11F3N2O11K).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Antifungal activity of a novel quercetin derivative bearing a
trifluoromethyl group on Candida albicans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tempesti, Tomas C.; Alvarez, M. Gabriela; de Araujo, Marcelo Francisco;
Aragao Catunda, Junior Francisco Eduardo; de Carvalho, Mario Geraldo;
Durantini, Edgardo N.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Medicinal Chemistry Research (2012), 21(9), 2217-2222

