$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2.2.2 4-(4-(4-nitrophenoxy) phenyl)-2, 6-diphenylpyridine (NPDP) In a
250-mL round-bottomed, two-necked flask equipped with a condenser, a
magnetic stirrer bar, a mixture of 3.24 g (0.01 mol) DPP, 1.41 g (0.01
mol) p-fluoronitrobenzene, and 1.50 g (0.01 mol) potassium carbonate in
40 mL DMAc was refluxed at 110°C for 12 h. During this time, the progress
of the reaction was followed by thin layer chromatography. The mixture
was then cooled and poured into 100 mL water and the yellow precipitate
was filtered, washed with water and dried in a vacuum oven. The yield of
the reaction was 90%. The product had melting point at 190-192°C. FT-IR
spectrum exhibited absorptions at 1547-1345 (NO2), 1244 (C-O-C), and 1603
cm-1 (C=N). Anal. Calcd. for C29H20N2O3: C, 78.37%,; H, 4.50%; N, 6.30.%.
Found, C, 78.45%; H, 4.56%; N, 6.22%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and Characterization of High Performance Poly(amide-imide)s
based on a New Diimide-diacid and Various Diamines
