$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the synthesis of
dibenzo[b,f]oxepine 10. A nitrogen-flushed microwave vial was equipped
with a magnetic stirring bar and charged with 4 Å molecular sieves (300
mg). The vial was flame dried for 10 min under high vacuum and purged
with N2. After cooling to 25 °C, the vial was charged with (2-
hydroxyphenyl)acetonitrile 8 (0.6 mmol), 2-bromobenzaldehyde 7 (0.72
mmol), Cs2CO3 (1.2 mmol, 2.0 equiv), and toluene (2.0 mL). The reaction
mixture was then heated at 130 or 150 °C. After 24-48 h, the mixture was
cooled to room temperature, filtered through a Celite pad, and washed
with CH2Cl2/EtOAc. The solution was concentrated under reduced pressure
and purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (20%
EtOAc/hexanes) to afford dibenzo[b,f]oxepine-10-carbonitrile.
6-Methoxy-3-methyldibenzo[b,f]oxepine-10-carbonitrile (10p). Reaction
time of 48 h. Yield 90%, yellow solid. Mp 143-144 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
acetone-d6) δ 7.69 (s, 1H), 7.34 (d, 1H, J = 7.9 Hz), 7.23-7.21 (m, 2H),
7.17 (s, 1H), 7.09-7.05 (m, 2H), 3.92 (s, 3H), 2.35 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (75
MHz, acetone-d6) δ 159.1, 153.3, 146.2, 145.0, 143.6, 131.3, 128.5,
127.1, 126.7, 126.7, 123.3, 119.6, 119.3, 115.3, 113.3, 56.7, 21.3; HRMS
(EI) calcd for C17H13NO2 [M+] 263.0946, found 263.0945.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM molecular sieves used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Transition-Metal-Free Synthesis of Dibenzo[b,f]oxepins from
2-Halobenzaldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Choi, Young Lok; Lim, Hye Sun; Lim, Hwan Jung; Heo, Jung-Nyoung
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(19), 5102-5105

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME124 STEP1
$RXN



