$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-[4-(3-aminophenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]biphenyl. A mixture of 3-aminophenol
(0.655 g, 6 mmol), 4-(4'- chlorobenzenesulfonyl)biphenyl (1.643 g, 5
mmol), potassium carbonate (0.829 g, 6 mmol), N,Ndimethylacetamide (DMAc,
30 mL) and toluene (10 mL)was heated to reflux under nitrogen, with
azeotropic distillation of water. After 3 h the toluene was distilled off
and the temperature was raised to 160 °C. After a further 4 h the
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, poured into water (200
mL), and the precipitate was filtered off. After washing with water and
methanol, the solid was dried at 80 °C for 2 h and purified by
chromatography (dichloromethane eluent) to give white solid. Yield: 1.8
g, 90% 4-[4-(3-aminophenoxy)benzenesulfonyl]biphenyl., yield 90% m.p.125
°C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 250 MHz) δ 7.99 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.90 (d, J = 9.0
Hz, 2H), 7.70 (d, J = 8.7Hz, 2H), 7.59 – 7.55 (m, 2H), 7.50 – 7.40 (m,
3H), 7.13 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.04 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.51 (dd, J =
8.0 and 2.2 Hz, 1H), 6.40 (dd, J = 8.0 and 2.2 Hz, 1H), 6.34 (t, J = 2.2
Hz, 1H), 3.76 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 62.5 MHz) δ 162.6, 156.4, 148.8,
146.4, 141.0, 139.6, 135.3, 131.2, 130.2, 129.5, 129.0, 128.6, 128.4,
128.3, 127.7, 118.2, 112.1, 110.5, 107.2; IR (Nujol): 3469, 3370 (νN-H),
1319, 1243 (νC-OC), 875, 828, 757 cm-1; MS (CI): m/z = 401 [M]+.
