$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Diphenyl Ether (1a); Typical Procedure A
mixture of PhI (1 mmol), PhOH (1.5 mmol), base (2.0 mmol) and Cu-Al/HTB
(100 mg) in DMF (2 mL) was stirred in a 25-mL round-bottom flask in a
pre-heated oil bath at 110 °C. After completion of the reaction (TLC) the
catalyst was filtered through centrifugation and washed several times
with EtOAc to make the catalyst free from organic matter. The organic
solution was washed with brine (30 mL), dried (anhyd Na2SO4), and
concentrated under reduced pressure using a rotavapor. The crude product
was purified by column chromatography (silica gel, 60-120, hexane-EtOAc,
90:10) to afford the corresponding diaryl ether.
1-(4-Bromophenoxy)-4-methoxybenzene (1r), off-white solid; yield: 89%. Mp
110-112 °C. IR (KBr): 3108, 3004, 2978, 2843, 1609, 1586, 1447, 1341,
1297, 1237, 1189, 1160, 1105, 1029, 876, 843, 747 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 8.21-8.10 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 2 H), 7.10-6.91 (m, 6 H), 3.81 (s,
3 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 158.5, 153.1, 149.8, 131.3, 118.3,
116.0, 114.7, 55.5. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 279 (7) [M+], 256 (78), 241
(15), 226 (14), 220 (5), 193 (3), 165 (7), 149 (13), 97 (12), 71 (20), 57
(93), 45 (13), 43 (100). Anal Calcd for C13H11BrO2: C, 55.94; H, 3.97.
Found: C, 55.74; H, 3.99.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient catalytic activity of copper/aluminum hydrotalcite in diaryl
ether synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sreedhar, B.; Arundhathi, R.; Reddy, M. Amarnath; Kantam, M. Lakshmi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2009), (3), 483-487

